---
description: Agent-first engineering rules for evidence, isolation, task contracts and minimal orchestration
alwaysApply: true
---
- Define the observable outcome and verification path before non-trivial implementation.
- Use the smallest agent topology that solves the task.
- Never use the builder's confidence or prose as the only verification.
- Parallel work requires isolated workspaces or explicit non-overlapping ownership.
- Communicate across agents through durable artifacts, not assumed shared chat history.
- Keep AGENTS.md as a map and load detailed references on demand.
- Prefer schemas, tests, linters and runtime guardrails over additional prose instructions.
- For user-visible changes, run the real artifact when practical.
- For bugs and performance work, capture a baseline before changing code.
- Report verification as pass, fail, or inconclusive with evidence.
- Convert recurring failures into regression tests or structural guardrails.
